mit a client operation with the real handlePropose (so the instance exists with bookkeeping and a pending proposal, status PREACCEPTED), then models the restart by constructing a fresh replica with no durable state, which is exactly what the launched configuration's durable=false implies; the recovery-led PreAccept then recreates the record without bookkeeping and the commit follows. Identity: the prerequisite record event and the commit result share instance 0.0. Oracle and limits: the panic is observed by wrapping only the commit delivery in recover, and the process-termination step remains an inference from the run loop having no recover, recorded as a limitation rather than observed; the same applies to the modelled restart, which is a construction of the state the configuration permits rather than an executed crash-restart cycle. No counterevidence was found that the handler survives in this scope.\\\",\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"the restart is modelled by a fresh replica rather than an executed crash-restart cycle, which the shipped durable=false configuration implies\\\",\n   \\\"the harness observes the panic; process termination follows from the run loop's lack of a recover and is an inference\\\",\n   \\\"one instance and one message pair are exercised\\\"]}]}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-review-c4b.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint(sub['artifact_id'])\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-review-c4b.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
